st=storypage('dhumra','SMOKE-EYES','Ślokas 6.1–24',
 panels('Three panels: the messenger reporting to Shumbha; Dhumralocana burnt to ash by a single sound; the lion destroying his army',[
  ('#fff3b0','THE REPORT','<rect x="20" y="50" width="70" height="80" fill="#ffd60a" stroke="#111"/>'+ASURA(55,130,.8,'#3a5a6a')+ASURA(120,170,.6,'#555')),
  ('#dfe9f6','“HUṂ”',DEVI(100,10,.5,False,'#fff')+T(50,60,'HUṂ!',20,'#c0392b')+''.join(f'<circle cx="{30+k*8}" cy="{140}" r="5" fill="#999" stroke="none"/>' for k in range(5))),
  ('#ffe3c4','THE LION',LION(72,130,.9))]),
 ['<b>The report.</b> The messenger tells Śumbha her answer. Furious, Śumbha orders Dhūmralocana: “Bring her by force, dragged by the hair. Kill anyone who protects her.”',
  '<b>The threat.</b> With 60,000 asuras he reaches the snowy mountain: “Come to my master willingly, or I drag you by your hair.”',
  '<b>Her reply.</b> “You are mighty, with an army; if you take me by force, what can I do?”',
  '<b>“Huṃ”.</b> He charges, and with that one sound she burns him to ash. Her arrows and her lion destroy his whole army in a moment.',
  '<b>Next.</b> Śumbha, lip trembling with rage, sends the great asuras Caṇḍa and Muṇḍa with a larger force.'],
 ("Sixty thousand soldiers, and the chapter is so short!","That's the point. Brute force doesn't even make a good story against her. The real battle is still ahead."),
 'Against her, brute force <b>doesn’t last a chapter</b>.')
P=dict(n=11,ch=6,out='/home/claude/work/devim/Devi_Mahatmya_Part11.html',
 title='Dhūmralocana · Part 11 · Devī Māhātmya series · srini.presents',
 desc='Devī Māhātmya, Part 11: chapter 6. Śumbha sends Dhūmralocana with sixty thousand asuras to drag the Goddess by the hair; she burns him to ash with the single sound “huṃ” and her lion destroys his army. Explained in plain English with illustrations.',
 h1='DHŪMRALOCANA',series='DEVĪ MĀHĀTMYA · PART 11 · CHAPTER 6',tag='Smoke-eyes and the syllable huṃ · explained and illustrated',cover=cover,
 how='The whole of chapter 6 <b>in full for chanting</b>, the story in <b>comic panels</b>, and the key ślokas on their own pages: the chant, a picture, what it says, the key words, one insight and the one thing to remember.',
 where=[f'In {plink(10)}, the gods sang “yā devī sarvabhūteṣu”. Kauśikī stepped out of Pārvatī, Śumbha proposed marriage, and she answered with her vow: “Whoever conquers me in battle shall be my husband.”',
  'Chapter 6 is short and sharp. Śumbha sends his general <b>Dhūmralocana</b>, “smoke-eyed”, to drag her by the hair. It is the first of four battles of the third carita, each against a stronger enemy.'],
 wtalk=("Why does she let them keep attacking?","It's a ladder. Each enemy is a harder one: Dhūmralocana, then Caṇḍa and Muṇḍa, then Raktabīja, then the brothers themselves. Watch how she answers each one."),
 fulls=[('CHAPTER 6 IN ONE GO','Ślokas 2–15',FV[:10]),('IN ONE GO · CONTINUED','Ślokas 16–24',FV[10:])],
 fulltoc='Chapter 6 in One Go',
 fullnote='Text as given in the Devīmāhātmyam edition of devimahatmyam.aurobharati.in (24 ślokas in chapter 6; speaker lines omitted); its numbering is followed.',
 seq=[st]+V,
 toc=[('THE STORY',[('dhumra','Smoke-Eyes')]),('THE KEY VERSES',V)],
 end=['<b>The order (6.2–5).</b> Hearing her vow, Śumbha orders Dhūmralocana to drag her by the hair and kill anyone who protects her.',
  '<b>The threat (6.7–9).</b> With 60,000 asuras: “Come willingly, or be dragged.”',
  '<b>The irony (6.11).</b> “You are so mighty; if you take me by force, what can I do?”',
  '<b>“Huṃ” (6.13–19).</b> One syllable turns him to ash; her lion destroys his army in a moment.',
  '<b>Next (6.20–24).</b> Śumbha, lip trembling, sends Caṇḍa and Muṇḍa with a bigger army.'],
 endsub='Chapter 6 in five lines',
 next=("What's next?",'Part 12: chapter 7. Out of the Goddess’s darkened brow leaps Kālī, garland of skulls, tongue lolling, who swallows elephants whole and brings back Caṇḍa and Muṇḍa. She gets a new name: Cāmuṇḍā.'),
 endkey='<b>one sound from her is enough</b>.',
 foot='Study notes on the Devī Māhātmya, chapter 6 (Mārkaṇḍeya Purāṇa). The chapter is given in full as in the Devīmāhātmyam edition of devimahatmyam.aurobharati.in, whose numbering is followed. The reading of huṃ as a mantra seed syllable is from later tradition. Meanings are our own plain-English renderings. Zappy and Prof. Bolt are fictional.')
